# The thinking map of the adk AgentHarness (docs/adr/0040 §2): what a
# role's THINKING (low|medium|high, plan §5) becomes in the request to
# each MODEL_PROVIDER. Read by lights_out_adk.model.thinking_map; a
# missing line is a refusal naming this file and the key. Each provider's
# three lines cite the page read and the date; the value is what the
# request carries, verified offline against google-adk 2.9.1 and litellm
# 1.106.6 (adapters/adk/lights_out_adk/tests/test_model.py).
#
# Gemini: google.genai ThinkingConfig.thinking_level, sent by ADK's
# BuiltInPlanner; gemini-3.8-flash accepts low|medium|high (AI Studio
# docs, "Thinking", https://aistudio.google.com/docs/thinking, read
# 2026-11-03).
GEMINI_LOW=low
GEMINI_MEDIUM=medium
GEMINI_HIGH=high
# Anthropic: LiteLLM reasoning_effort, which litellm 1.106.6 sends as
# thinking {type: adaptive} plus output_config.effort; the Claude API
# accepts low|medium|high|xhigh|max on every current model (Claude
# Platform docs, "Effort",
# https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/effort, read
# 2026-11-03). Three levels stay three (plan §5).
ANTHROPIC_LOW=low
ANTHROPIC_MEDIUM=medium
ANTHROPIC_HIGH=high
# OpenAI: LiteLLM reasoning_effort, sent unchanged as the Chat
# Completions reasoning_effort; low|medium|high are accepted by every
# current reasoning model, none|minimal|xhigh|max are model-dependent
# (OpenAI docs, "Reasoning",
# https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/reasoning, read
# 2026-11-03).
OPENAI_LOW=low
OPENAI_MEDIUM=medium
OPENAI_HIGH=high
